{"t": 1794781585558, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "recruit_hidden", "Recruiting is invisible on screen: next to a stranger pawn the button row offers only nation-level actions (Propose Alliance / Gift Lowerham 25 coins / Declare War), with no Invite or Gift-pawn button. Invite (R) and Gift (G) are only on page 1 of the ? Controls screen. Also, the pawn name tag sits behind the Chronicle panel (top middle), so the player can't see who they're chasing."]}
{"t": 1794781586204, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "pawns_all_leaders", "By day 1 afternoon (tick ~8400) nearly every wandering pawn has declared or founded its own one-person nation (chronicle lists 20+ nations: Lowerham, Villageport, Townshire, Oldton, Blackburg...). Tilly Smith: 'I lead Lowerham. We are 1 strong.' This empties the pool of recruitable strangers just when the Village era needs 10 members; after the 2 auto-joins at founding I gained no members."]}
{"t": 1794781586868, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "invite3", "Pawns are hard to reach for E/R: pt walkto pawn timed out or got 'stuck: not getting closer' 6 of 8 tries because wandering pawns move about as fast as the walking player at 1-2 fps; when I did reach Tilly Smith, she walked out of the 5-unit reach before the next key press. R then said 'There is no one within reach to invite.' (tick 8432)."]}
